synopsis: Add RFC 10008 QUERY and Accept-Query support
prs:
issues: #1900
significance: significant
description: {

Add `Query` and its status aliases (`QueryAccepted`, `QueryNonAuthoritative`, `QueryNoContent`, `QueryResetContent`, and `QueryPartialContent`), covering all six standard Query status forms across `Verb`, `NoContentVerb`, `UVerb`, `MultiVerb`, and `Stream`, including the generic server, client, documentation, foreign, and quickcheck paths. Required request content can be composed with `ReqBody`.

Expose typed `AcceptQuery` and `AcceptQueryHeader` support in `Servant.API.AcceptQuery`. Swagger 2 and OpenAPI 3 remain compile-time unsupported because neither format has a `QUERY` operation.

The `servant` package now requires `http-types >=0.13 && <0.14`; release is blocked until upstream `http-types` 0.13 is available.
}
